Backbone: frozen MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593 at revision            
f826b80d2822, already fine-tuned on AudioSet, whose 527 labels include all ten  
ESC-10 categories. Training adapted only the new classifier head (its LayerNorm 
and linear layer); 'initial' is that head at its seeded random initialization,  
and 'majority' always predicts the most frequent training class. Scope: 80 test 
clips from 57 source recordings on this fixed split (ESC-50 folds 1-3 train, 4  
validation, 5 test) with one training seed (42). These are point estimates, not 
the five-fold ESC benchmark, and clips from one source recording are correlated.
AudioSet category coverage is known; whether any of these recordings were also  
in the backbone's training data is unresolved. The original AudioSet classifier 
is not evaluated here, so beating the random head is not an improvement over    
pretrained AST. Softmax is uncalibrated; synthetic additive noise is not        
evidence of real-world noise robustness. Candidate: this run is evidence for    
maintainer review, not automatic release approval.                              
